Krita Nova 36 - Photoshop-style Character and Paragraph panels (text tool, part 1)

Two new dockers (Settings > Dockers > Character / Paragraph, docked on the
right by default), laid out like Photoshop's panels, for the text being
edited. They use the same text property models as the Text Properties
docker, which stays for everything else ("More Text Options..." shows it).

Character - the selected characters while some are selected in the text,
otherwise the whole text (or the defaults for new text):
- font family, style (weight / width / slant / named instances);
- size (tT) | leading (A↕, with Auto = the font's normal line height);
- kerning (Metrics / None) | tracking (VA, letter spacing);
- baseline shift (Aª) | color (the foreground color, which the text tool
  applies to the selection; click to choose);
- bold, italic, all caps, small caps, superscript, subscript, underline,
  strikethrough;
- OpenType: standard ligatures (fi), discretionary (st), historical (ct),
  swash (A, 'swsh'), stylistic alternates (aa, 'salt'), titling (T),
  ordinals (1st), fractions (½).

Paragraph - the whole text:
- align left / center / right, justify with the last line left / centered /
  right, justify all (text-align-all, text-align-last; text-anchor for point
  text);
- direction left to right / right to left;
- first line indent (hanging);
- Roman hanging punctuation.

Not in SVG text, so not in the panels: vertical / horizontal character
scaling, left / right paragraph indents, space before / after paragraphs,
hyphenation.

Files: NovaTextPanelDock.{h,cpp} (the dock: QML host, text color, More
options), qml/NovaCharacterPanel.qml, NovaParagraphPanel.qml and the small
NovaLengthField, NovaLeadingField, NovaToggle; registered in
TextPropertiesPlugin.cpp, textproperties.qrc, CMakeLists.txt.
